    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup faces a mixed slate today, but two players clearly separate themselves as the primary offensive engines. **Kyle Tucker** (74.59) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) are our top plays, both benefiting immensely from plus-matchups against subpar pitching. **Kyle Tucker** is set to feast on the favorable xERA of Gasser, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** exploits a high-upside platoon advantage against Holmes, G. **Sam Antonacci** (66.81) also demands attention; his spot at the top of the order combined with a 0.397 xwOBA makes him a high-floor leadoff option against Houser, whose 4.67 xERA invites significant damage.\n\nWe are forced to navigate some tactical volatility elsewhere. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (48.73) remains in the lineup despite a daunting matchup against Skenes (2.96 xERA); while the SP skill penalty is severe, his base talent and favorable park factors keep him just above our bench threshold. Conversely, **Nolan Schanuel** (41.64) is our most difficult bench decision. He was nearly slotted into the lineup, but his inability to clear the efficiency bar against a tough arm like Eovaldi (3.19 xERA) pushed him to the reserves. **Gunnar Henderson** would normally be a lock, but he is sidelined today due to a rainout. With **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Robert Jr.** both dealing with injury designations, the roster depth is being tested, making it vital for **Andy Pages** (68.07) and **Josh Jung** (61.16) to capitalize on their exploitable matchups to sustain our weekly efficiency targets.",
